# Shell scripts, systemd units and the Caddyfile are executed by bash/systemd on
# Linux. A CRLF line ending is invisible in a diff and fatal at runtime: bash
# reads `set -euo pipefail\r` as an invalid option name and exits 2.
#
# That is not hypothetical. ops/iridium/sync-tailnet-host.sh was committed with
# CRLF and, when it started failing, it took the dashboard deploy down with it
# mid-run -- after the Caddyfile had been installed but before Caddy was
# restarted, leaving the host serving a config three minutes older than the file
# on disk. The face routes looked ungated in /etc/caddy/nova.Caddyfile while the
# running Caddy still gated them, which is a genuinely confusing state to debug.
*.sh      text eol=lf
*.service text eol=lf
Caddyfile  text eol=lf
*.Caddyfile text eol=lf
